ow I mean a lot of the  emotional scenes we have  um are not only sort of vulnerable for  the characters but I think just very  vulnerable topics in general that would  really require the you know friendship  that the two of them have so that stuff  I mean it I don't know it felt very real  on the day and that and that hopefully  led to both of our performances  yeah and I love that about this film  that there was those very real moments  that people can relate to and you guys  really do it with ease now Amaya do you  toss and turn at night before the day  you have to film a big scene like an  exorcism is that something that you get  nervous about or embrace it I didn't  even sleep last night because I had to  do this today  so exorcism scenes that's even worse no  I don't sleep and it's so annoying  anytime I have something to do or  something I care about is the next day I  it it's I might as well like drink an  energy drink like yeah just keep the  train rolling yeah yeah  I love that I'm sure you probably  transfer that into your performance too  which is kind of cool if I'm guessing  right but yeah I was so tired that I  just it was easier to cry  I love that oh now Elsie Switching gears  a bit I'm super jealous you post on  Instagram couple months ago you got sent  gifts from Nintendo  um have you had the chance to play Zelda  breath of the wild it is it as good as  they say that's the question I have for  you oh definitely breath of the wild I  think that's like one of the I that was  one of the first games I got on my  switch  um uh and I really didn't touch it for a  long time because I wasn't like a Zelda  fan and then I fell so deeply into it  um and that was one of the things I  played on set a lot for this I always  had my switch and I would do like Mario  I I always had a little switch her  switch and a notebook to write whatever  she was thinking or did little Doodles  she was so cute and I would just I know  I was listening to music  it's like  I love that  um now Amaya at such a young age being  really the poster you know face for this  huge film and War of the Planet of the  Apes or for the Planet of the Apes is  there something you learned from that  experience that you've kind of taken  with you with these projects you're  doing now  oh my gosh yeah so much of everything I  know now is because of that movie I  worked with some of the most incredible  actors and even like the Press tour that  I went on from that you know like stuff  like this it helps me with that so many  lessons were learned because of that and  so many friendships were made and  it's kind of I was talking about this  the other day because I did that when I  was 11 and kind of new to this industry  and it just set the bar for everything  else and  yeah so it's that movie has such a  special place in my heart I love it  that's awesome yeah and it's a great  movie and everyone loves that movie make  sure to check out Amaya and I'll see  crush it like they always do in My Best  Friend's exorcism which is out tomorrow  on Prime video thank you guys for  joining me today and I hope to talk to  you in the future yeah thank you man

